  clock: 2  # 6b0d
  nonce: 6b0d  # 6b0d
  message: "FIXED in PR #1251 (merge pending cron confirmation; see below).\n\nTHE ROW'S UNCHECKED QUESTION, ANSWERED: scip-python's tests DID execute in the scheduled suite, by accident. Clean env without the package: collecting its tests alone gives 5 ImportErrors (rc=2); collecting core's tests first makes them import. Bisection over core's test files isolates test_adjudication_packet.py, which loads scripts/measure-taint-precision.py at collection time; that script inserts every packages/*/src into sys.path. So the package ran uninstalled (no entry point, so no analyzer registration), unmeasured (no --cov), one unrelated edit away from collection errors. The CI log for full-suite @ cc3a7cab confirms: no hypergumbo_lang_scip_python in its coverage table.\n\nDone: .woodpecker/full-suite.yml test-all-packages and nightly.yml test-matrix install it and --cov it. check-package-coverage scip-python: 100% in isolation.\n\nLint scanners, measured (the row's premise was partly wrong): check-docstring-drift DID skip it (default co-change scan 352 -> 359 files). The other four (check-id-construction, check-pass-id-agreement, check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration, check-recorded-producer-input) held the list only as a sys.path import fallback; they scan packages/*/src or packages/*/tests by glob, or discover analyzers via installed entry points (scip_python IS in the registry under the venv). They now glob, so there is no list to forget; all exit 0.\n\nStructural: tests/test_ci_package_lists.py derives the set from the tree and pins every Woodpecker step whose pytest runs packages/*/tests/ (install set + cov == cov-paths.sh) and each linter's resulting sys.path (run in a subprocess). Mutation: old full-suite.yml fails 2, old check-pass-id-agreement fails 1.\n\nNOT changed: .github/workflows/{ci,full-suite,nightly}.yml. GitHub Actions is disabled under Woodpecker CI (scripts/ci-debug; no GitHub context reports on dev commits), and they already lag (several install blocks lack rust-analyzer too). Also untouched: full-suite's self-tree-validation / self-claims-gate and nightly's integration steps, which run no package tests (adding a backend package there could move the self-tree baseline; not measured).\n\nTo close: the next Woodpecker full-suite cron on a commit containing this must be green with scip-python in its coverage table."  # 6b0d
